      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: FBT locomotion work fine. This issue can still persist today because it come from the rig itself not a bug. V3 is more sensible with bone orientation. From that picture, we can see that the bone in the leg are strait from the front view yes, but they probably have not roll set to 0. So the IK is confuse which way to bend. That's why you get those floppy leg motion. If I guess from the description since the video is gone.",
